-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sabatino</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lihatsh</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Adler</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Swig</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dark</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Thoughts associated with unprotected anal intercourse among men at high risk in San Francisco 1997-1999</article-title><source>Psychol. Health</source><year>2002</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>246</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-ijerph-06-01620"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mansergh</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Marks</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Colfax</surname><given-names>GN</given-names></name><name><surname>Guzman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rader</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchbinder</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>&#x02018;Barebacking&#x02019; in a diverse sample of men who have sex with men</article-title><source>AIDS</source><year>2002</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>653</fpage><lpage>659</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11873010</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijerph-06-01620"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Theodore</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Duran</surname><given-names>REF</given-names></name><name><surname>Antoni</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intimacy and sexual behavior among HIV-positive men who have sex with men in primary relationships</article-title>