/lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17331279</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21-ijerph-06-01620"><label>21.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrino</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowen</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hernandez</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Cardenas</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rehbein</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Club drug use, sexual behavior, and HIV risk among community and internet samples of Hispanic MSM: Implications for clinicians</article-title><source>J. Soc. Work Practice Addict</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>100</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22-ijerph-06-01620"><label>22.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rhodes</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hergenrather</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Yee</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramsey</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparing MSM in the southeastern United States who participated in an HIV prevention chat room-based outreach intervention and those who did not: How different are the baseline HIV-risk profiles?</article-title><source>Health Educ. Res</source><year>2008</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>180</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17412716</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b23-ijerph-06-01620"><label>23.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malebranche</surname><given-names>DJ</given-name