de-sex: White masculinities and &#x02018;authentic&#x02019; heterosexuality among dudes who have sex with dudes</article-title><source>Sexualities</source><year>2008</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>414</fpage><lpage>434</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b27-ijerph-06-01620"><label>27.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosek</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An exploration of the down-low identity: Nongay-identified young African-American men who have sex with men</article-title><source>J. Natl. Med. Assn</source><year>2005</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>1103</fpage><lpage>1112</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b28-ijerph-06-01620"><label>28.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mays</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cochran</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Zamudio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV prevention research: Are we meeting the needs of African American men who have sex with men?</article-title><source>J. Black Psychol</source><year>2004</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>78</fpage><lpage>105</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b29-ijerph-06-01620"><label>29.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rhodes</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hergenrather</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Yee</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Knipper</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkin</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Omli</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characteristics of a sample of men who have sex with men, recruited from gay bars and internet chat rooms, who report methamphetamine use</article-title><source>AIDS Patient Care STDs</source><year>2007</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>575</fpage><lpage>583</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17711382</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b30-ijerph-06-01620"><label>30.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Correlates of substance use in relation to sexual behavior in black gay and bisexual men: Implications for HIV prevention</article-title><source>J. Black Psychol</source><year>2008</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>70</fpage><lpage>93</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b31-ijerph-06-01620"><label>31.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aguinaldo</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Myers</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A discursive approach to disinhibition theory: The normalization of unsafe sex among gay men</article-title><source>Qual. Health Res</source><year>2008</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>181</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18216337</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b32-ijerph-06-01620"><label>32.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parsons</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV-positive gay and bisexual men</article-title><source>Positive prevention: Reducing HIV transmission among people living with HIV/AIDS</source><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Kalichman</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><publisher-name>Kluwer Academic/Plenum Publishers</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, USA</publisher-loc><year>2005</year><fpage>9